================================================================================
GAME SPECIFICATION: SKY RAID 1942
Vertical arcade shooter in the style of 1942
Single-file Python 3 + Pygame + NumPy
================================================================================

1. PURPOSE
----------
A 1942-like vertical scrolling space shooter. Player at the bottom, enemies
from the top. Formations, bosses, power-ups, fire/spark/explosion particles,
attract mode (story crawl, high scores, CPU demo), resizable window with
saved geometry, high-score persistence, cheat key, synthesized SFX/music.

2. PLATFORM / CONSTRAINTS
-------------------------
- Language: Python 3.9+
- Libraries: pygame, numpy
- One source file (e.g. c3041.py)
- Virtual resolution VW=480, VH=720, 60 FPS
- Window: pygame.RESIZABLE. Letterbox-scale the 480x720 surface to the
  window (smoothscale, black bars, keep aspect).
- Persist to skyraid_save.json beside the script:
    { "width", "height", "x", "y", "highscores": [["NAME", score], ...] }
  Save size/position on resize, periodically (~1.5s), and on quit.
- Restore size on launch. Set SDL_VIDEO_WINDOW_POS before set_mode if x,y
  known. Do NOT use pygame._sdl2.video.Window on macOS (crash).
- AUDIO ON macOS: never call pygame.mixer.init() or pygame.mixer.Sound /
  sndarray. Write 16-bit mono 22050 Hz WAV files to .skyraid_sfx/ and play
  with /usr/bin/afplay via subprocess (cap ~8 concurrent). Loop music in a
  daemon thread of afplay. Other OSes may use pygame.mixer + WAV files.
- pygame.init() then set_mode. Fonts: SysFont("consolas") with Font(None)
  fallback.

3. CONTROLS
-----------
Move: Arrow keys or WASD
Shoot: Space (hold to fire continuously, subject to fire_delay)
Start new game from attract/game-over: Space or Enter
Unlimited lives toggle (in play only): U
Quit: Esc or window close
High-score initials: Left/Right select letter, Up/Down or type A-Z/0-9,
  Backspace, Enter confirms

4. ATTRACT / FLOW
-----------------
Startup mode = story.
Cycle until player starts:

  A. STORY CRAWL
     Starfield background. Yellow Star-Wars-style crawl: lines start near
     the bottom at scale 1.0, move up, shrink toward a vanishing point
     (y≈78) down to 1/8 original size, fade as they near the horizon and
     the bottom edge. Title "SKY RAID" and subtitle fade out over time.
     Hint blinks: "PRESS SPACE / ENTER TO START"
     Stay until the LAST non-empty story line has reached ≤1/8 scale AND
     is above the lower screen, OR player starts. Play theme music.

  B. HIGH SCORES ("HALL OF ACES")
     20 seconds. Theme music continues. Top 10 names + scores. Rank 1 gold.
     Same start hint.

  C. DEMO
     Stop theme. CPU plays a real session until a boss has finished
     *entering* (boss_seen) or player dies. Then back to story + music.
     50% of demos: player.max_upgrades() (4-way shot, spread, fire_delay=4,
     huge shield, speed 6.4, 9 lives). All demos: unlimited lives.
     Overlay "DEMO" and start hint.

Start (Space/Enter) from story, scores, demo, or game-over:
  clear particles, Session(demo=False), mode=play, stop theme.

Play ends (lives=0, not unlimited):
  If score beats 10th place (or list short) and score>0: initials entry,
  then insert and save, then story.
  Else: story.

5. STORY TEXT
-------------
Title: SKY RAID
Episode line: A long time into the war...

Body (scroll these lines; blank lines are spacers only):
  The outer colonies have gone dark.
  From the rust-red moons of Vesper to the
  ice docks of Faraday, every beacon has
  been swallowed by a fleet that does not
  negotiate and does not leave survivors.

  They call themselves the Crimson Armada.
  Their carriers blot out suns. Their
  fighters move in living flocks, stitched
  together by a single cold intelligence
  buried in the flagship NEMESIS.

  Earth is next.

  The last squadrons burned in orbit.
  The admiralty is ash. All that remains
  is one patched interceptor, a handful of
  stolen warheads, and a pilot who refused
  the order to retreat.

  You are that pilot.

  Climb the well. Cut through the flocks.
  Break their captains. When the sky itself
  catches fire, keep climbing.

  If Nemesis reaches the blue world below,
  there will be no second story.

  The raid begins now.

Crawl: origin starts at VH+30, origin -= 0.85 per frame.
line_y = origin + index * 28
scale = lerp(1.0, 0.125, p) where
  p = clamp((VH-50-line_y)/(VH-50-78), 0, 1)
Color ≈ (255, 210, 70). Perspective shrink via smoothscale.

6. LOOK / WORLD
---------------
Clear color (8,10,28). Soft dark ellipses as "clouds" drifting down.
~90 stars: random x, speed 1.2–5.5, brightness 80–255, wrap to top.
Ships are polygons: pointed body, two wings, cockpit ellipse.
Player colors: body (40,200,255), wing (20,90,180), cockpit (180,255,255),
  accent white. Enemies use varied palettes (red, orange, purple, green,
  pink, blue). Enemies drawn flipped (nose down). Damaged ships
  (hp < 45% max) emit fire/smoke trails.

Particles:
  spark: short bright yellow/orange lines, high velocity
  fire: upward orange/red circles, shrink
  smoke: gray circles that grow and rise
  debris: gray/rust fragments
burst() on hits/deaths; fire_trail() on player engines and wounded hulls.

7. PLAYER
---------
Size ~28x32, start (VW/2, VH-80), speed 5.2, clamp to screen.
lives=3, score=0, fire_delay=10 frames, multi=1, spread=False, shield=0,
invuln=0, unlimited=False.
Shoot: bullets color (80,255,255), vy=-11.
  multi 1: one shot; 2: x±8; 3: -12,0,12; 4: -16,-6,6,16
  spread adds two green shots vx=±3.2, vy=-9
Hit: if invuln>0 ignore; if shield>0 spend 90 shield + sparks;
  else big burst, lose a life (unless unlimited), invuln=90, multi-=1
  (min 1), lose spread, fire_delay = min(10, fire_delay+2). Blink while
  invuln. Shield drawn as pulsing green circle.
U toggles unlimited; if enabling, force alive and lives>=1.
HUD bottom: SCORE 0000000   LIVES n|INF   WAVE w
  plus MULTI/SPREAD/RAPID/SHIELD/CHEAT flags if active.
Collision box slightly inset vs enemy bullets/bodies/boss.

8. POWER-UPS
------------
Drop ~12% from killed normal enemies; 3 random drops from dead boss.
Fall vy=1.6. Circle + letter: M multi, R rapid, S shield, L life, S spread
(use kind[0]; multi cyan, rapid gold, shield green, life pink, spread purple).
On pickup:
  multi: multi = min(4, multi+1)
  rapid: fire_delay = max(4, fire_delay-2)
  shield: shield = 360 frames
  life: lives += 1
  spread: spread = True

9. ENEMIES
----------
Types:
  scout        22x22 hp1 score50  spd3.2  one red shot down
  fighter      26x26 hp2 score80  spd2.4  twin orange shots
  tank         34x30 hp5 score160 spd1.5  aimed magenta shot at player
  bomber       40x28 hp4 score140 spd1.8  3-way gold shots vx -2,0,2
  interceptor  24x24 hp2 score70  spd2.6  one pink shot
Shoot cooldown random 50–140 after firing; only if on-screen and player
exists. Flash white 4 frames when hurt. HP bar if max_hp>2.
Paths: down; sine (base_x + sin(t*0.08)*70); zag (x += cos(t*0.12)*3);
  dive (faster + steer 2% toward player x); circle (cos(t*0.06)*60, y+=1.2).
Despawn y > VH+40.

10. FORMATIONS (wave % 7)
-------------------------
0 V-flock of 7 (scout early, fighter after wave 2), sine, staggered Y
1 Dual side streams of 8 scouts each, zag
2 Wall of 6 (fighter, tank after wave 4), down
3 6 interceptors circle, phase offset
4 5 dive bombers
5 Mixed stream of 10 cycling all kinds, sine
6 Pincer: 5 fighters each side dive + 1 center tank down

After a wave is cleared, wait 50 frames, wave+=1.
If wave % 4 == 0: spawn Boss(level=wave//4) instead of a formation.
After a boss dies: wave already incremented, wait 90 frames, then formation.

11. BOSSES
----------
level starts at 1. Size ~90+8*level by 60+4*level. hp=40+25*level.
score=1500*level. Enters from y=-80 until y>=110. Then patrol
  x = VW/2 + sin(t*0.025)*(140+8*level)
  y = 110 + sin(t*0.04)*18
Wide hull + wings. Top-screen HP bar labeled BOSS n.
At half HP, fire trails on both sides.
Fire every max(16, 50-4*level) frames. Pattern (t//90 + level) % 4:
  0 fan of 7 red shots
  1 8-way radial orange
  2 3 aimed violet shots at player
  3 spawn scout/fighter minion if enemies<10 + two teal shots
Death: 8 large mixed bursts + 3 power-ups.

12. DEMO AI
-----------
Priority: (1) dodge predicted enemy bullets that reach player y within 28
frames and overlap ±26 px, and overlapping enemy bodies;
(2) intercept reachable power-ups (prefer multi/spread/rapid/shield);
(3) line up under nearest on-screen enemy (lead sine/zag/circle), prefer
tanks/bombers; or under boss;
(4) otherwise drift center / sit low.
Always fire. Stay in bounds.

13. HIGH SCORES
---------------
Default table: REX 25000, NOVA 18000, KAI 12000, MIRA 9000, JON 7000,
VAL 5000, ASH 3500, REN 2000, PIO 1000, ACE 500.
Keep 10, sort descending. Initials 3 chars, stored uppercased (allow up
to 8 in file). Name entry screen: "NEW HIGH SCORE" + score + three slots.

14. SOUND
---------
Generate waveforms, write WAV, play as specified in §2.
  shot     square 880Hz 60ms
  enemy    sine 220Hz 80ms
  explode  noise 80Hz 280ms
  hit      noise 160Hz 90ms
  power    sine 660Hz 180ms
  boss     square 110Hz 400ms
  death    noise 70Hz 500ms
Theme: short minor/heroic melody (G3 B3 D4 G4 F#4 G4 E4 D4 C4 D4 E4 G4
F4 E4 D4 …) with attack/decay envelopes + light harmonics, then pause,
loop during story and high-score only. Stop on play/demo. Restart on
return to story.

15. IMPLEMENTATION NOTES FOR AN LLM
-----------------------------------
- Keep simulation in virtual 480x720; only blit scaled.
- Session object owns player, bullets, enemies, powers, boss, wave, state
  ("play"|"boss"|"between"|"gameover").
- Particles are a global list shared by bursts and trails.
- Do not block the game loop on audio. afplay must be async; music stop
  must terminate the looping process.
- No external art or sound assets other than generated WAVs and JSON.
- Visual tone: colorful geometric fighters, lots of things to shoot,
  fire/sparks/explosions, choreographed flocks — not photorealistic.
================================================================================